;; What was measured on 2026-09-09 while porting the whole of aadhaar.main to
;; one Kotoba component, and what was NOT. The `:blocked` disposition this
;; repo's migration-record.edn carried rests on a gap table measured on
;; 2026-09-03; most of that table does not reproduce, and the part that DOES
;; reproduce is not the part the table named.
{:as-of "2026-09-09"

 :amu-which-amu
 "Measured in a clean worktree of kotoba-lang/amu at 6ffc1d71, which is the
  west pin 24516340 plus two commits (the pin is an ancestor; verified with
  git merge-base --is-ancestor). The 2026-09-03 table was measured against
  57ba0ee0 and a later partial re-measurement against 13acc443, so three
  different amu shas are in play across the three rounds and the sha is named
  on every claim below rather than assumed."

 :loader
 "tools/kexe_loader.c built FROM THE SAME WORKTREE, not from
  orgs/kotoba-lang/amu. The shared checkout was verified to carry KEXE_FUEL
  support as well (grep -c KEXE_FUEL = 3 in both), so the two agree here, but
  the worktree copy is the one that was built and run."

 ;; ------------------------------------------------------------------
 :what-differs-from-the-com-aave-sibling
 ;; The task framing was that this is the same generated REST-actor template
 ;; and the diff should be small. It is NOT small in the way that matters.
 ;; `diff src/aave/main.cljc src/aadhaar/main.cljc` was run; here is what it
 ;; actually showed.
 {:entities-4-vs-6 "aave has four entity specs, aadhaar has six."

  :refs-empty-vs-live
  "EVERY aave spec is :refs {}. FIVE OF SIX aadhaar specs carry
   :refs {:identityId \"Identity\"}. In aave the `expand` fold was therefore
   dead on the production path and its port could only be exercised by handing
   it a SYNTHETIC refs table. Here `handle-get` reaches it with the real table
   for Credential, Consent, Transaction, Document and VerificationRequest. This
   is a layer that is genuinely exercised here and was not there."

  :float-absent-vs-reached
  "aave coerces nothing to :float, so its missing as-float was a public
   function of the oracle that NOTHING IN THE COMPONENT REACHED. aadhaar's
   Transaction spec is :coerce {:amount :float}, and `amount` is also one of
   Transaction's two REQUIRED fields. So the blocked layer is on the
   create/update path of one of the six entities. This is the materially
   bigger gap, and it is stated loudly under :as-float below."

  :kernels-present-vs-absent
  "aave.main additionally defines as-int-kernel, clamp-limit and
   has-more-kernel? as public functions, kept beside page-limit for a retired
   slice. aadhaar.main defines NONE of them. They are therefore absent from
   this port on purpose: porting them would be inventing a surface the oracle
   does not have."

  :otherwise-identical
  "Beyond the ns docstring, ns-prefix, the entity-specs table, the healthz
   actor string and the start! keyword, the two .cljc files are byte-identical
   in structure. So the framing was right about the template and wrong about
   the size of the difference."}

 ;; ------------------------------------------------------------------
 :capability-imports
 ;; ADR-q9: a clock or an entropy source crosses as a DECLARED CAPABILITY
 ;; IMPORT and is not a reason to keep a component in Clojure.
 {:clock/now {:wire-id 7 :status :pass}
  :entropy/draw {:wire-id 23 :status :pass}
  :form "(ns … (:capabilities #{:clock/now :entropy/draw})) then (clock/now x)"
  :policy "{:allow #{[:cap/call 7] [:cap/call 23]}}"
  :probe "q9-probes/g24-capability-stub.kotoba"

  :what-the-grant-actually-answers
  "seed + 1, for BOTH capabilities. Measured over five seeds: 0->1, 1->2,
   2->3, 5->6, 100->101. The com-aave component header says the granted
   clock/now 'answers 1'; that is true only at seed 0, and this port's header
   was corrected rather than carrying the claim forward."

  :measured-in-both-directions
  "With the grant WITHDRAWN (loader capability argument `-`), both calls answer
   KEXE_TRAP {:kind :signal :signal :SIGTRAP}, exit 120. This is the control
   that matters: without it, a stub that ignored the policy entirely would look
   identical to a capability that is really being granted."

  :consequence
  "`now` and `rand-hex16` are therefore exercised at a STUB instant.
   oracle-clock and oracle-entropy are determinism checks on the artifact, NOT
   parity checks against aadhaar.main, whose `now` reads a real clock and whose
   `rand-hex16` reads a real UUID. Neither is reproducible by construction."}

