 :not-measured
 {:the-clj-arm-of-as-int
  "The one mismatch rests on Long/parseLong throwing on '12abc'. That arm was
   NOT executed -- this is a JVM-free exercise. Read from source, not run."

  :fuel-required-by-this-component
  "Every execution was run at KEXE_FUEL=100000000, chosen for being large. A
   structured report on one call showed 99986767 remaining of 100000000, so
   that call used about 13000 -- but the per-layer requirement was not
   measured, so nothing here says what budget a host would have to grant."

  :the-wasm-and-web-targets
  "Only aarch64-macos was compiled. The refusal message names kotoba-script web
   and typed Wasm as targets that DO carry typed values, so a :document-carried
   version -- and possibly as-float itself -- may well compile there. Not tried,
   so the as-float gap is a gap in THIS target, not proven to be a gap in the
   language."

  :the-json-scanner-on-adversarial-input
  "Escape DECODING is not implemented: a string value containing a backslash is
   read as its raw bytes. Every fixture here is escape-free ASCII. Behaviour on
   escaped or non-ASCII input is untested."

  :row-count-ceiling
  "arr-count-from stops at 64 and key-count-from at 32. No store larger than
   five rows was executed, so the behaviour at those ceilings is untested."

  :the-other-five-entities-end-to-end
  "Handler probes drive Identity, and the expand probes drive Credential. The
   table, refs and route hashes cover all six entities, but Consent,
   Transaction, Document and VerificationRequest were not driven through
   create/list/get/update/delete end to end. Notably that means the float arm
   was probed directly but NOT through handle-create on a Transaction."

  :consumer-cutover
  "Nothing was cut over. aadhaar.main remains the oracle and nothing requires
   aadhaar.whole-component. This is a whole-component BUILD that runs, not a
   completed migration."}}
